A||||3||BBBAD GT||4cyl Fuel Pump Questions and V8||||1||
Z||000000||BBBAD GT||05-06-2001||06:10 PM||||Well, coming home from Bob's and the V8 Fiero starting cuting out and died twice on the Interstate.  Let her sit a while, and it fires back up.  Got her to Effingham and I parked her for the night until I can get it next morning.  Good thing the Hot Rod Power Tour was there for the night, or else I wouldn't have had anything to look at until the wife came.....<P>Anyway, I'm almost sure its the fuel pump (or the ignition, but prob not), and I'm wondering if the 4 cyl fuel pump normally dead heads into the iron duke's induction (TB fuel injected? I'm not sure).  What pressure does the pump with the 4 cyl normally run at?  <BR>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">         <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A><BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 05-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||85Josh||05-06-2001||08:59 PM||||The normal pressure for the Duke's TBI is 9-13 PSI. It does use a return line for excess fuel. Are you running it into a carb with no return? If so, you have probably burned the pump from not relieving pressure. <P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||05-07-2001||12:14 AM||||If you are running the pump with no return line or pressure regulator you may be seeing fuel pressures as high as 18 psi.  This is the maximum "dead head" pressure according to my shop manual.  If you are using a carburetor on your V8 you may be overpowering the needle valve and overfilling the float chamber which will make it run extremely rich.  Most carbs are designed to operate with around 5 pounds of fuel pressure at the carb inlet.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||4
Z||000003||BBBAD GT||05-08-2001||01:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85Josh:<BR><B>The normal pressure for the Duke's TBI is 9-13 PSI. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats what I needed to know.  The setup right now is just the 17 yr old 4 cyl pump going to the 5.5lb regulator (supplied in the Archie kit), and then to the carb with no return.  If the original pump's operating range is only 9-13, then I won't lose any sleep just replacing the pump.  This is the way the Archie's kit intends it to work with a carb.  ||||reg||1
